<h1 class="text-center underline underline-offset-4 text-3xl font-medium mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

<%# Each answer is a card; keep questions short and answers plain. %>
<% card = "block max-w-2xl mx-auto rounded-lg bg-white p-6 shadow-lg dark:bg-neutral-700 mb-4" %>
<% link = "underline text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-900 dark:text-teal-300 dark:hover:text-teal-100" %>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">Where does the species information come from?</h2>
  <p>
    The species catalog is gathered automatically from Wikipedia's lists of freshwater and marine
    aquarium fish, invertebrates, plants and amphibians. Names, sizes, water types, notes and pictures
    are taken as Wikipedia has them.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">I found a mistake in a species. How do I fix it?</h2>
  <p>
    Please correct it on Wikipedia. Catalog species can't be edited on Aquatanks: the catalog is
    refreshed from Wikipedia, so a fix made there reaches everyone here on the next update, while an
    edit made here would be overwritten. The Wikipedia lists we use:
  </p>
  <%# Keep in step with SpeciesScraper::PAGES in db/seeds.rb %>
  <ul class="list-disc ml-6 mt-2">
    <% %w[freshwater_aquarium_fish brackish_aquarium_fish marine_aquarium_fish
          freshwater_aquarium_invertebrate marine_aquarium_invertebrate
          freshwater_aquarium_plant marine_aquarium_plant freshwater_aquarium_amphibian].each do |page| %>
      <li><%= link_to "List of #{page.tr('_', ' ')} species", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_#{page}_species", class: link, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">A species I keep isn't in the catalog. Can I add it?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes. Logged-in users can add a <strong>custom species</strong>, from the
    <%= link_to "species page", species_index_path, class: link %> or from "Add a custom species" under
    a tank's add box. Custom species are yours alone: they're marked "Custom", only you can edit or delete
    them, and they never change the official catalog. Other people only see one if it's stocked in a tank
    they're allowed to see.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">Who can see my tanks and photos?</h2>
  <p>
    Public tanks can be seen by anyone, logged in or not. A private tank, and its photo, is visible only to
    you. You choose this per tank ("Visible to other users"), and set the default for new tanks on your
    Profile. Your name, profile picture and public tanks are shown on your tanks page.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">Why is a species in my tank flagged for the wrong water?</h2>
  <p>
    Each catalog species lists the water it prefers: freshwater, brackish or saltwater. When that doesn't
    match your tank's water type, the tank page warns you. It's a reminder rather than a rule; some
    species tolerate more than one, and some appear in the catalog once per water type.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">What photos can I upload?</h2>
  <p>
    JPEG, PNG, WebP or GIF images up to 10 MB, for a tank's main photo, its gallery (up to 30 photos of your
    setup and livestock, added on the tank page) or your profile picture. Gallery photos follow the tank's
    privacy setting. iPhone HEIC photos
    aren't supported yet; most phones convert to JPEG when you share or export a photo.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="<%= card %>">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-medium mb-2">Can I use metric units, dark mode or scientific names?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes. Your <% if logged_in? %><%= link_to "Profile", edit_user_path(current_user), class: link %><% else %>Profile<% end %>
    has preferences for units (gallons or litres), theme, results per page, showing scientific names first,
    and a default water type for the catalog.
  </p>
</section>
